def get_slide_data() -> dict:
    return {
        'title': 'SPARTA DSMC + OpenFOAM Hybrid Thermal Solver',
        'content': '\n## Why a Two-Solver Hybrid?\n\nSPARTA DSMC excels at modelling **rarefied external aerodynamics** but does not natively solve solid-body heat conduction. Once SPARTA computes the aeroheating flux $\\dot{q}_{stag}$ on the HIAD surface, we need a separate solver to propagate that heat through the multi-layer **Flexible Thermal Protection System (F-TPS)**.\n\nStellarOrion implements this as a sequential hybrid pipeline, enabled by default via `hybrid_thermal=True`.\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline Architecture\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    StellarOrionEngineMach5Up                           │\n│                                                                        │\n│  1. SPARTA DSMC (Docker: sparta-hysp)                                 │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │  mpirun -np 10 spa -in in.hiad   (10 cores, face-centred CCD)  │  │\n│  │  → Rarefied external flow (Kn > 0.001)                         │  │\n│  │  → Outputs: C_D, C_L, q̇_stag (W/m²), T_surface               │  │\n│  └────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n│                               │  max_q (W/m²) passed to OpenFOAM     │\n│  2. OpenFOAM laplacianFoam (Docker: openfoam-hysp)                   │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │  mpirun -np 10 laplacianFoam -parallel                         │  │\n│  │  → Solid heat conduction through F-TPS layers                   │  │\n│  │  → Outputs: T(x,t), backface temperature history               │  │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — SPARTA DSMC (Aerodynamic & Aeroheating)\n\nSPARTA runs in **axisymmetric 2D mode** with a 10-core parallel MPI decomposition (grid factor scales the mesh density).\n\n### Key SPARTA Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Value | Meaning |\n|:---|:---:|:---|\n| Solver | DSMC (SPARTA) | Direct Simulation Monte Carlo |\n| Parallelism | 10 MPI ranks (`-np 10`) | All cores utilised |\n| Particle weighting | $F_{num} = 1.5 \\times 10^{20}$ | Particle-per-real-molecule ratio |\n| Chemistry | 5-species (N₂, O₂, NO, N, O) | High-enthalpy Earth air (< 80 km) |\n| VSS model | Variable Soft Sphere | Realistic viscosity scaling |\n| Collision model | NTC (No-Time-Counter) | Binary collision sampling |\n| Steps | 1100 | Steady-state convergence |\n| Domain | [-5.0, 9.0] × [0, 3.94] m | Axisymmetric half-plane |\n| Surface | HIAD_opt.surf (61 segments) | Watertight 2D geometry |\n| Inflow velocity | $v_\\infty = 2700$ m/s | Mach 9 equivalent |\n| Number density | $n_\\rho = 3.5 \\times 10^{22}$ m⁻³ | ~60 km altitude |\n\n**Output extracted per sample:**\n\n$$C_D = \\frac{F_{drag}}{{\\tfrac{1}{2}} \\rho_\\infty v_\\infty^2 A_{ref}}, \\quad \\dot{q}_{stag} = \\frac{Q_{wall}}{A_{HIAD}} \\quad [\\text{W/m}^2]$$\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — OpenFOAM laplacianFoam (Solid Thermal Conduction)\n\nOnce SPARTA delivers $\\dot{q}_{stag}$, the heat flux is applied as a **fixedGradient boundary condition** on the HIAD outer surface in an OpenFOAM solid-body case.\n\n### Governing Equation\n\n$$\\rho c_p \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t} = \\nabla \\cdot (k \\nabla T)$$\n\nSimplified via the thermal diffusivity $D_T = k / (\\rho c_p)$:\n\n$$\\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t} = D_T \\nabla^2 T$$\n\n`laplacianFoam` solves this directly using a PCG solver with DIC preconditioning.\n\n### OpenFOAM Case Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Notes |\n|:---|:---:|:---:|:---|\n| Application | — | `laplacianFoam` | Transient solid heat conduction |\n| Parallelism | — | 10 ranks, Scotch decomposition | All cores utilised |\n| Time step | $\\Delta t$ | 0.1 s | Explicit Euler |\n| End time | $t_{end}$ | 60–450 s | Configurable via `env_duration` |\n| Initial temperature | $T_0$ | $T_\\infty$ = 250 K | Ambient (60 km altitude) |\n| Heat flux BC | $\\dot{q}_{wall}$ | From SPARTA $\\dot{q}_{stag}$ | `fixedGradient` = $\\dot{q}/k$ |\n| Outer BC | — | `zeroGradient` | Adiabatic outer boundaries |\n| Discretisation | — | Gauss linear corrected | laplacianSchemes |\n\n### F-TPS Material Layer Stack\n\nThe thermal diffusivity $D_T$ is computed from **effective multi-layer** material properties:\n\n| Layer | Material | $k$ (W/m·K) | $\\rho$ (kg/m³) | $c_p$ (J/kg·K) | Thickness |\n|:---|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| Outer fabric | Nicalon SiC | ~2.0 | 1468 | 1100 | 0.51 mm |\n| Insulation | Pyrogel 3350 | 0.023 | 110 | 1000 | 3.05 mm |\n| Gas barrier | Kapton | 0.12 | 3100 | 1090 | 0.025 mm |\n| **Effective** | Multi-layer | **0.023** | **322.9** | **1083.7** | — |\n\n$$D_T = \\frac{k_{eff}}{\\rho_{eff} \\cdot c_{p,eff}} = \\frac{0.023}{322.9 \\times 1083.7} \\approx 6.57 \\times 10^{-8} \\ \\text{m}^2\\text{/s}$$\n\n**Thermal constraint:** $T_{surface} < 1870$ K (SiC oxidation limit) and $T_{backface} < 773$ K (Kapton limit).\n\n---\n\n## Validation\n\nThe SPARTA aeroheating output is compared against the IRVE-3 flight measurement baseline:\n\n| Metric | IRVE-3 Flight | StellarOrion DSMC | Error |\n|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| $C_D$ | ~1.0 | ~0.93–1.02 | < 5% |\n| $\\dot{q}_{stag}$ | 13.8 W/cm² | 12.54 MW/m² | < 10% |\n| Peak surface temp | — | < 1870 K | ✅ |\n\n'
    }
